    "Maintain your current loading and progression scheme — all lifts are trending upward, so do not change what is working. Add small increments of weight or reps where you feel capable rather than making large jumps.",
    "Add one extra set of direct biceps work next period, such as a fourth set of curls, to begin closing the volume gap between biceps and triceps and support balanced arm development.",
    "Consider adding one additional shoulder isolation exercise or an extra set to your shoulder work, bringing it closer to 5 to 6 sets next period for more balanced upper body development.",
    "Continue monitoring recovery between sessions. The strength gains are strong across the board, but sustaining this rate of progress requires adequate sleep and nutrition — make sure protein intake remains sufficient to support muscle growth at your body weight."
  ],
  "contextSummary": "Outstanding period with strength index gains across all six muscle groups, particularly legs, chest, and back; volume is well-distributed with mild underdevelopment in biceps and shoulders worth addressing next period."
}
